{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_2c40dd9364f2f178b782bfddf5f21143e4f8831ab90ee4dd648f0348c912b830"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Authentication is handled by passing an authenticated Snowpark session, created with standard Snowflake connection parameters, to the gateway and its tools."},{"claim_ids":["clm_37de4c1411acb67cefa0a66299b55fee0b2383dfbba4da1721f77c274c6d91d7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Rather than forcing users to choose between Cortex Search RAG and Cortex Analyst Text2SQL, the gateway routes each request to the appropriate tool."},{"claim_ids":["clm_512ae7d1a9db19ca531a9bc83a7874c76b591647898c50904ad277d1aac525f5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The framework supports four tool types: Cortex Search for unstructured data, Cortex Analyst for structured data, Python for custom operations such as third-party API calls, and SQL for custom user-built SQL pipelines."},{"claim_ids":["clm_58ebf11e4fbd1a97d37e384f31f0be3aa5e0dc16a128f4a8b789624d14b9f5f4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An Agent is constructed with a snowflake_connection and a tools list, and is invoked by calling it directly with a natural-language question string."},{"claim_ids":["clm_60d1aeeb1bf95a4db105f8bd31861c53907cef1fd5987d7b3a1a7b3d4986b201"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tools are instantiated from classes including CortexSearchTool, CortexAnalystTool, PythonTool, and SQLTool, configured with metadata such as service_name, semantic_model, tool_description, and a Snowpark session."},{"claim_ids":["clm_643c1d58cf32bba0fc82d260c095d1521773cb567b17bb9f2024a3817092f9e2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The package installs via pip as orchestration-framework and is documented for Python 3.10 or 3.11 in a new virtual environment."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6ac89ab9f6d3e38383bcec97331e611a132ecd376c975548764d78d8d12a99cb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A dedicated planner LLM decomposes the user's request into an execution plan, forming a task graph that invokes tool calls asynchronously and in parallel where possible, with Snowflake compute used for plan generation and tool execution."},{"claim_ids":["clm_790fca3cb7d2ecfb533067a1c55f13198e3bf65ebcb9eb8f33d90321c00caa36"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The gateway logs at INFO level by default to show which tools answer a question, with LOGGING_LEVEL=DEBUG for more detail, and an optional Trulens integration (orchestration-framework[trulens]) provides execution traces via a TruAgent class."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7988f614b6d56876947c527af7c537e7dabcf8d1ffdbbc927b01ed9a237e4feb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Agent Gateway is described as an agentic orchestration framework offering native support for Snowflake tools."},{"claim_ids":["clm_85f4fda2e5440eb415122e6395464e63805a998efcf0a3a00775e68f89da8014"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agents require the underlying Cortex Search, Cortex Analyst, SQL, or Python tools to be configured by the user before use."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d46995aa72fa0ac1ad62f0e83cfbdc13c5d80c684e3b247f642edeb8a787bbde"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The architecture is stated to leverage the LLM Compiler design from Berkeley AI Research Lab, citing a 2024 paper on parallel function calling."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e59012651ea124b7b6a04f836ff0f8d29b7d0be7d6852c9f29b38b46519c56c8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Multiple tools of the same type, and tools in different Snowflake accounts or schemas via separate Snowpark sessions, appear attachable to a single agent."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f87c1c3355267fa0e355173bfbb9d9de2fa403ac540cd7f55e22bc87fc555e8b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The library is optimized for client-side orchestration; for orchestration managed inside Snowflake, the README recommends the Snowflake Cortex Agent API instead."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fd4cf707c517f3af8bb79dfb735f4fd12b8431989f64510984373e208bb11d31"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The gateway can run in SPCS and Snowflake notebooks, requiring an external access integration network rule for direct GitHub or PyPI installation."}],"claim_ids":["clm_2c40dd9364f2f178b782bfddf5f21143e4f8831ab90ee4dd648f0348c912b830","clm_37de4c1411acb67cefa0a66299b55fee0b2383dfbba4da1721f77c274c6d91d7","clm_512ae7d1a9db19ca531a9bc83a7874c76b591647898c50904ad277d1aac525f5","clm_58ebf11e4fbd1a97d37e384f31f0be3aa5e0dc16a128f4a8b789624d14b9f5f4","clm_60d1aeeb1bf95a4db105f8bd31861c53907cef1fd5987d7b3a1a7b3d4986b201","clm_643c1d58cf32bba0fc82d260c095d1521773cb567b17bb9f2024a3817092f9e2","clm_6ac89ab9f6d3e38383bcec97331e611a132ecd376c975548764d78d8d12a99cb","clm_790fca3cb7d2ecfb533067a1c55f13198e3bf65ebcb9eb8f33d90321c00caa36","clm_7988f614b6d56876947c527af7c537e7dabcf8d1ffdbbc927b01ed9a237e4feb","clm_85f4fda2e5440eb415122e6395464e63805a998efcf0a3a00775e68f89da8014","clm_d46995aa72fa0ac1ad62f0e83cfbdc13c5d80c684e3b247f642edeb8a787bbde","clm_e59012651ea124b7b6a04f836ff0f8d29b7d0be7d6852c9f29b38b46519c56c8","clm_f87c1c3355267fa0e355173bfbb9d9de2fa403ac540cd7f55e22bc87fc555e8b","clm_fd4cf707c517f3af8bb79dfb735f4fd12b8431989f64510984373e208bb11d31"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:22:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_ff7694cc95814166b02442e638e117e3","id":"pg_5a0a5240382459e880ca86d8ffb5c968","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/snowflake-labs-orchestration-framework-readme-md-9addb6d4b303-86d8ffb5c968.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_c0b2117589155b4da269322fcfcfbcdf"],"title":"Snowflake-Labs/orchestration-framework/README.md @ 9addb6d4b303","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:22:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ff7694cc95814166b02442e638e117e3"}
